WEBVTT

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.950
"The Dancer on the Bridge"

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.950
Does anyone have any questions up to this point?

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.660
I don't seem to see Lucian here.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.160
Is he absent again today?

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.200
Professor!

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.830
What is it, Tate?

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.950
He's-- Lucian, um... has a cold.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.410
Oh, is that so?

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.500
Very well, after the lecture,
I think I shall go visit him.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.700
Th-That's all right! Lucian and I
share the same dormitory room,

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.290
and I'm looking after him, so...

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.450
Indeed.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.790
Well then, that is a relief.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.000
As you wish. Tate Percival
and Lucian Atwood, yes?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.290
Hmm?

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:49.120
Lucian is the heir to Atwood Viscountcy,
a noble family of over two centuries.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.250
Tate is likewise...

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.540
So both of them are heirs
to aristocratic families.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.750
Honestly, where have you gone?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.290
I can't cover for you any longer.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.250
Now <i>I'm </i>coming down with a cold.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.950
Yes?

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.080
P-Professor Moriarty!

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.500
That was quite the sneeze.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.040
I heard it all the way outside the door.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:32.790
Have you been looking after Lucian
and caught his cold from him?

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:36.160
Er... quite possibly.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.450
Um, I, uh...

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.580
This isn't...

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.750
There is no sign that this bed
has been slept in for some time.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.410
You should start talking, quickly.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:58.330
Right now, I am a hundredfold
more cross than you may think.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.540
So Lucian has not been home in three days?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:12.120
There have been times when he would
go behind the housemaster's back,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.450
stay out all night, and sneak
back in the next morning,

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.160
but he has never done this before.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:21.790
So this has made me rather worried,
prompting me to go to the pub where Frida,

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:25.620
this waitress for whom he is
head over heels, works.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.790
If there is anyplace he would spend the night,
I expect it would have to be her place.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.500
Get out!

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.040
I see. That would explain your sneezing.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.830
However, for you to receive such
a harsh welcome without warning,

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.120
there may have been some trouble beforehand.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:57.120
He... does have some foolhardy and philandering
ways, but he's a good egg at heart.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.250
If he's... If he's mixed up
in any sort of trouble...

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.790
...then I have to do something.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.290
You seem to be quite concerned for Lucian.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.120
Of course I am, sir!

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.750
Of course?

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.040
I mean, he's...

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.290
...my friend, after all!

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.540
Tate, it's best that you remain
out of this matter from now on.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:29.450
Huh?

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.750
Please allow me to deal with Lucian.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.330
V-Very well.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.830
Also...

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:43.790
...always treasure this feeling
of fondness for your friend.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.290
Professor Moriarty, I presume?

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.700
And you are...?

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:00.700
The name is Dudley Bale.
I assist with the administration here.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.450
I have seen you on the campus from time to time,

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:08.500
but this is the first time
I've introduced myself.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.790
I saw you coming from the student dormitories.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:13.330
Is there something amiss
with one of the students?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.330
Oh, no. Lucian Atwood, one of the
students who attends my lectures,

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.870
has been absent for several days,
so I went to go visit him in his room.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.410
Did you find him moaning with a hangover?

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:28.370
He was not in his room. According to the
student with whom he shares the room,

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:31.080
he has not been back for three days now.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.700
Oh dear, staying out overnight
without permission, is he?

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:36.950
I realise that he cannot help being
young, but this is still troubling.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.660
On the other hand, why don't we
look the other way this time?

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:46.120
If we come down on them too hard,
they are liable to find us suffocating.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:50.870
Still, to be gone for three whole days
is a tad unusual, is it not?

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.750
Perhaps we should contact the police.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:57.620
The police, you say? I cannot concur with that.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.830
Lucian is a son of nobility.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:03.830
A brush with the law may reflect
poorly on the family name.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.250
So you would have us leave the matter alone?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.540
No, no, not at all. You may not
believe it by looking at me,

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:13.410
but I have a bit of influence
with the local police.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:18.290
Allow me to take the matter from here
and discreetly look into it.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:22.330
So, as you can see, there is
nothing for you to worry about.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:26.620
This is the pub that Tate mentioned.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.500
We're not open yet.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.160
Yes, I am aware.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.500
I am not here to drink today.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.040
I am here to have a word with you.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:48.120
Quite the tip just for talking
about a dead girl.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.040
Are you a newspaper reporter?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:57.410
No. I am William James Moriarty.
I teach at Dunham University.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.330
You're a college professor?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:05.290
If there is an issue with a student's conduct,
it is my duty as an educator to set it right.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:10.830
To that end, I thought I should gather
all the facts of the matter.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:16.950
Frida truly was a fine girl.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:21.370
She was a good dancer, and when she smiled,
the whole room would light up--

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.450
a real flower of a girl.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.700
So I can't believe what happened to her.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.370
From what the old man who
lived under the bridge said,

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:39.870
she was singing and dancing atop
the bridge before she fell in the river.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:43.660
What, I wonder, could she have been singing?

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:53.370
Frida and your student had
fallen in love with each other.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:59.120
But he's a big-deal aristocrat.
Not of the same status as us.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:04.160
So I'm sure she thought he was
just playing games at first.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.500
However, he then proposed marriage to her.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.660
Huh?

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:16.370
I want to spend the rest of my days
dancing with you... on the stage of life.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:20.410
Would you object to having me...
as your dance partner?

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:26.750
Lucian...

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.080
I tried to stop her at first. But then...

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:35.620
...she told me that she was with child.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.450
But even more than that, when I saw
that blissful look on her face,

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.250
I found myself unable to raise any objections.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:46.660
But before long, <i>he </i>came into the picture.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:51.910
I don't know what he said to Frida... but...

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:59.620
...I could tell that she had been abandoned.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:06.080
Even so, she gathered herself up,
and said she would raise the child alone.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.540
But then...

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.500
Forgive me for making you
recount such a harrowing tale.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:18.540
However, with your assistance,
I now know what must be done.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.370
I do not know if it will meet your expectations,

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:26.290
but I promise that I will do everything
in my power to resolve this matter.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.040
Just a moment, there!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:34.830
Frida's remains are buried
in the potter's field.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.450
Unfortunately, with our earnings,

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:40.790
we could not so much as afford
a proper grave for her.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:48.000
If you feel any pity for the girl, use that
to place some flowers on her grave.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.620
Where is the package I entrusted to you?

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:41.200
The goods we procured from that new line
of stock appear to be quite potent.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.700
He's resting comfortably inside.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.290
Are we feeling more composed today, Lucian?

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.870
Frida...

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:05.790
Unfortunately, she had a little accident
and died. Fell right into the river.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:10.580
I... made Frida... a promise...

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:13.080
You may not be able to accept this just yet,

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:17.660
so you should just stay here and rest
until your emotional wounds have healed.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:20.830
That's it. No rush.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.250
Louis...

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.250
Send those two a telegram for me.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:36.950
Then you mean...

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.200
It is time for us to make our move.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.450
Tch.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.120
Telegram, sir.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:39.790
I appreciate you coming all the
way down here to greet me.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.040
It has been a long time, Colonel Moran.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:47.620
We're finally getting started, right?
That's why you called me here, eh?

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:52.200
Now, now, take it easy.
Everything in its proper order.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.790
Incidentally... I trust your skills
have not grown rusty.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.790
A silly question.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.290
Yo, Fred!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.120
I see you're just as amiable as ever.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.160
I asked Fred to come in ahead of you.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.330
Did you locate what I asked you to find?

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:15.450
He wasn't in the hospital, but rather
the brothel two doors down.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:20.290
I believe that thanks to the opium,
he is still not in his right mind.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:23.000
It appears that everything is ready.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:28.500
There is no client for this job. However...

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.540
Now, let's go deliver some punishment.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.950
Looks like I win again.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:54.950
Wow! Mr Moran, you're so good!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:58.450
It's all mine. I'm having a nice streak of luck.

00:15:58.450 --> 00:15:59.620
Luck, you say?!

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.700
You sure you're not just cheating?!

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:08.330
That's what everyone who's
down on their luck says.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:12.000
On the battlefield, those were
the blokes that died first.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.250
Tch.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:17.540
So, Mr Moran, sir, now that
you've made all that money,

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.700
how about we have a different sort of fun?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.160
Good idea.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.910
Is your room on the second floor here?

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:25.870
Yes, and you're quick to catch my meaning.

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:28.620
You caught my eye as soon as I came in here.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.330
Oh, Mr Moran...!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.160
Where am I?

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:51.080
Lucian!

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.660
Sir Dudley?

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.410
Was it you? Were you the one?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.660
Did you summon me to come here?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.660
Huh?

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:08.410
What is the meaning of that letter?!
You're going to confess your crime?

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:11.000
After everything I did to clean up after you?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:14.790
For that matter, how did you
even get out of your room?!

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.790
Clean up after me...?

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:18.080
Yes!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:22.080
How could you get that common woman
pregnant? Bloody careless of you!

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:24.790
Which is why I had to go to such effort!

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:29.620
Frida...?

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.620
You are a nobleman!

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:36.330
That backwater dishrag of a woman
is no one for you to trip up over!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.250
Do you not understand that?!

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:41.580
You toss out the piece of paper if you
make a slip of the pen, don't you?

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.120
People are the same way!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.450
That is the way of the
aristocratic world you live in!

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:51.000
I meant... I meant to marry Frida...

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:55.750
That is quite enough of that!
Hold your tongue and do exactly as I say!

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.830
Lucian...

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.200
I-Impossible! You're...!

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:14.870
I-I pumped you full of opium, and you
plunged to your death in the river!

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.160
Huh?

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:26.040
At last, we hear it from your own mouth--
the confession of the unpardonable sin.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:29.040
P-Professor Moriarty?

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.660
Fred, that will do.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.870
Right.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.160
A-A man?!

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:40.540
Fortunately, the fog is heavy this evening.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:44.080
He may be smallish and sleight of build,
but when you look more closely...

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:48.500
So that's it! You're the one
who called me out here!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:53.500
Correct. I am the one who plotted all of this.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:59.870
I, William James Moriarty, Crime Consultant.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:03.910
Consultant? What is the meaning of this?

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:09.620
Mr Bale, I did a little checking, and in
addition to administering the university,

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:14.870
you are the owner of several
hospitals--no, make that brothels.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:17.290
S-So what if I am?

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:20.540
By means of your "hospitals,"
you will not arouse suspicions

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:25.750
by acquiring sizeable quantities of opiates
under the pretence of medicinal purposes.

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:32.000
Then you use said opiates to turn the cellars
of your brothels into opium dens.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.830
You entice the sons of aristocrats
to indulge in evil pleasures,

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:37.330
then demand that their parents
purchase your silence

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:41.250
if they do not wish those
deeds to be made public.

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:45.910
You go about setting fires, then offer
your services as the fire brigade.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.950
You are quite the scoundrel.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.910
Ha! You know that much, do you?

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:54.120
So, do you mean to turn me over to the police?

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:56.120
No, I'm not doing that.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:00.660
It seems that your claim to have influence
with the police was not entirely without merit.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.540
So what <i>are </i>you going to do?

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:09.000
You are going to taste the guilt that comes
from driving Miss Macaulay to her death,

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.950
and dance in a frenzy
before taking your own life.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:18.910
Huh? Me, commit suicide?
Are you touched in the head, Moriar--?

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:22.790
Huh? What the--?

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.040
Quite a nice step, there.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.330
I am sure your dance partner
will be quite satisfied.

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:48.330
Your partner by the name of Death.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:50.540
Stop! Don't do this!

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.540
Make it stop!

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:40.000
The kid erected a fine tombstone, didn't he?

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.750
A love impermissible
due to difference in status.

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:45.580
Yeah, a tragic tale.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:50.040
Both Frida and the kid are victims
of the country's class system.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:55.250
In a different world, the two of them
would have found happiness.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:57.160
Quite right.

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:01.580
Which is why...

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:04.450
...we must change it.

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:11.250
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:15.450
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:34.540
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:40.290
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:47.040
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:50.660
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:50.660 --> 00:22:54.410
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:59.250
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:02.910
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.580
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
<i>at the end</i>

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:09.540
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:13.790
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:20.370
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:21.870
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:28.700
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:34.370
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:36.750
<i>There is no turning back</i>

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:51.870
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Adventure of the Noahtic, Act 1."
